{"study_accession":"PRJNA684605","secondary_study_accession":"SRP297701","title":"ERYTHROID MITOCHONDRIAL RETENTION TRIGGERS MYELOID-DEPENDENT TYPE I INTERFERON IN HUMAN SLE","description":"Using both in vitro-derived RBCs as well as RBCs isolated from SLE and CANDLE patients we were able to demonstrate that a defective proteasome activation during human erythropoiesis leads to the generation of pro-inflammatory RBCs that retain mitochondria. Overall design: RNA-seq of PBMC from SLE patients and RBCs derived from PBMC from healthy donors and SLE patients. RBC group definitions: Mito- RBCs group are PBMCs from SLE patients that do not carry mitochondria inside their RBCs (Red blood cells) Mito+ RBCs : Ops IgG- group are PBMCs from SLE patients that carry mitochondria inside their RBCs (Red blood cells) and they don't have opsonizing anti-RBCs IgG in their plasma Mito+ RBCs : Ops IgG+ group are PBMCs from SLE patients that carry mitochondria inside their RBCs (Red blood cells) and they have opsonizing anti-RBCs IgG in their plasma","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":23,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN17062196","study_accession":"PRJNA684605","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"cDNA7035","description":"cDNA7035","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM4971718","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-08-25","attributes":[["source_name","PBMCs isolated from SLE patients"],["patient diagnosis","SLE"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["condition","Mito+ RBCs : Ops IgG- group"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13243296","experiment_accession":"SRX9675055","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":22354295,"base_count":3353144250,"first_public":"2021-08-25","experiment_title":"NextSeq 500 sequencing: GSM4971718: cDNA7035 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN17062197","study_accession":"PRJNA684605","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"cDNA7034",